From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kai Krakow <kai@kaishome.de>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 22:29:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia: retry explicit big-page sysmem allocations with
 smaller pages

sysmemConstruct() walks down the page sizes on NV_ERR_NO_MEMORY only
when the client left the page size at its default. A client that asks
for NVOS32_ATTR_PAGE_SIZE_BIG or _HUGE explicitly gets the error back
as soon as the OS has no free block of that order, which is the normal
state of a desktop after some uptime: pageblocks fill up with unmovable
allocations and compaction cannot rebuild order-9 blocks any more.

Seen with Marvel's Guardians of the Galaxy under vkd3d-proton after
20 h uptime, 5.7 GB free but no free order-9 block even after a manual
compaction. The user-space driver's sysmem allocations failed with

  NVRM: ... Out of memory [NV_ERR_NO_MEMORY] (0x00000051) returned from _memdescAllocInternal(pMemDesc) @ mem_desc.c:1354
  NVRM: ... Out of memory [NV_ERR_NO_MEMORY] (0x00000051) returned from rmStatus @ system_mem.c:460

four times within 60 ms, and the game exited a second later. Without
the dxgi.maxDeviceMemory workaround this happened while loading the
game world; with VKD3D_CONFIG=no_upload_hvv after 24 minutes.

Retry these requests with the next smaller page size as well, using the
existing loop. Smaller physical pages don't break the client's mappings:
dmaAllocMapping_GM107() maps memory at its physical page size when a
larger mapping page size is requested for non-contiguous memory. The
client also gets the page size it ended up with back in attr/attr2, as
with the default page size path.

Contiguous allocations are left alone, they need one block of the
whole size regardless of the page size. Clients that set
NVOS32_ATTR2_FAIL_FAST (UVM) already retry themselves.

As in the default path, the attempts before the last one are fail-fast,
so an explicit 2M request no longer stalls in direct compaction before
falling back. Each fallback is logged at LEVEL_ERROR, the only level
release builds print, because the client gets smaller pages than it
asked for.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 673e452ebf4dd73d63e2f4d94a5841d434eaf1cf)
---
 src/nvidia/src/kernel/mem_mgr/system_mem.c | 34 ++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/nvidia/src/kernel/mem_mgr/system_mem.c b/src/nvidia/src/kernel/mem_mgr/system_mem.c
index 7e88506b..4fe65a18 100644
--- a/src/nvidia/src/kernel/mem_mgr/system_mem.c
+++ b/src/nvidia/src/kernel/mem_mgr/system_mem.c
@@ -192,6 +192,7 @@ sysmemConstruct_IMPL
     NvU32 flags;
     RM_ATTR_PAGE_SIZE pageSizeAttr;
     NvBool bRetry = NV_FALSE;
+    NvBool bExplicitPageSize = NV_FALSE;
     NvBool bLockAcquired = NV_FALSE;
     NvBool bPrevSkipIommuMapping = NV_FALSE;
 
@@ -281,7 +282,7 @@ sysmemConstruct_IMPL
     }
 
     //
-    // Enable retrying the allocation only if the page size is default.
+    // Enable retrying the allocation if the page size is default.
     // Each new attempt decreases the page size to the next supported RM value
     // until the minimum OS granularity is reached.
     //
@@ -290,6 +291,22 @@ sysmemConstruct_IMPL
     {
         bRetry = NV_TRUE;
     }
+    else if ((FLD_TEST_DRF(OS32, _ATTR, _PAGE_SIZE, _BIG, pAllocData->attr) ||
+              FLD_TEST_DRF(OS32, _ATTR, _PAGE_SIZE, _HUGE, pAllocData->attr)) &&
+             !FLD_TEST_DRF(OS32, _ATTR, _PHYSICALITY, _CONTIGUOUS, pAllocData->attr) &&
+             !FLD_TEST_DRF(OS32, _ATTR2, _FAIL_FAST, _YES, pAllocData->attr2))
+    {
+        //
+        // Explicit big or huge page requests fail when the OS has no free
+        // block of that order, which is common after some uptime. Retry them
+        // with smaller pages, too: a mapping requested at a larger page size
+        // than the physical one falls back to the physical page size in
+        // dmaAllocMapping_GM107(). Contiguous allocations need one block of
+        // the whole size either way, and fail-fast clients retry themselves.
+        //
+        bRetry = NV_TRUE;
+        bExplicitPageSize = NV_TRUE;
+    }
 
     do
     {
@@ -443,7 +460,20 @@ sysmemConstruct_IMPL
                 {
                     NV_CHECK_OK_OR_GOTO(rmStatus, LEVEL_ERROR, rmStatus, failed_destroy_memdesc);
                 }
-                NV_PRINTF(LEVEL_INFO, "Sysmem alloc failed, retrying with page size 0x%llx.\n", pageSize);
+                if (bExplicitPageSize)
+                {
+                    //
+                    // Release builds only print LEVEL_ERROR. The client gets
+                    // smaller pages than it asked for, which is worth seeing.
+                    //
+                    NV_PRINTF(LEVEL_ERROR,
+                              "Sysmem alloc of 0x%llx bytes with page size 0x%llx failed, retrying with page size 0x%llx.\n",
+                              pAllocData->size, memdescGetPageSize(pMemDesc, AT_GPU), pageSize);
+                }
+                else
+                {
+                    NV_PRINTF(LEVEL_INFO, "Sysmem alloc failed, retrying with page size 0x%llx.\n", pageSize);
+                }
 
                 // Freeing memdescs to avoid leaks on retry.
                 memdescFree(pMemDesc);
